	)
	(text_box "Everything runs from the 5 V of USB PROG (or a bench 5 V on J601, diode-OR'd).\nTwo switching regulators make the digital 3.3 V (FPGA I/O, SDRAM, flash, PHY, FTDI) and the 1.1 V core,\nin the far corner from the converters. Every analog rail is its own LDO off the 5 V: +3V3_ADC, +3V3_DAC;\nthe op amps get +5VA through a ferrite bead and -4.2 V from an LM27761 charge pump (then a bead).\nThe converters' digital supplies and the PHY take +3V3 through beads, so their noise stays off the common rail.\nFerrite beads, simulated (sim/pdn_bead.cir): each bead's ~1 µH resonates with its 10 µF at ~50 kHz, a 0.7 Ω\npeak seen by the load -- far below the 1.5 and 2 MHz switchers (5 mΩ there), and no regulator loop sits behind a bead.\nBudget: FPGA ~0.6 W, ADC 0.6 W, DAC 0.4 W, PHY 0.4 W, FTDI 0.3 W, amplifiers 0.4 W, SDRAM 0.2 W: about 3 W, 0.6 A at 5 V."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 20.32 25.4 0)
		(size 124.46 17.78)
		(margins 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525)
		(stroke
			(width 0)
			(type default)
		)
		(fill
			(type color)
			(color 255 255 194 1)
		)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.1 1.1)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "85e2c336-a3ee-c4bc-b9b0-ddca7e7e9611")
	)
	(text_box "Sequencing (FPGA-DS-02012 §3.5, Master SPI): VCCIO8 must be above the flash's VIH before the FIRST of VCC\nand VCCAUX reaches its POR threshold, or PROGRAMN/INITN must be held low until it is.\nHere VCCAUX is an LDO off +3V3 (= VCCIO8), so it cannot lead it; VCC is the other buck, enabled by the same\n5 V with the same soft-start; and the 100 nF on PROGRAMN (FPGA sheet) holds configuration off for ~0.5 ms\nafter +3V3 is up in any case. Scope +3V3 against +1V1 on the first board.\nThe PHY, converters and amplifiers tolerate any order."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 20.32 317.5 0)
		(size 95.25 12.7)
		(margins 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525)
		(stroke
			(width 0)
			(type default)
		)
		(fill
			(type color)
			(color 255 255 194 1)
		)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 0.95 0.95)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "d2987b30-2957-319e-26d2-8adcc0537dd2")
	)
